Lessons from earlier runs:
- [plan] An end-to-end input timer can fail because the browser withholds rAF even when input handling and the commit each cost under a millisecond.
- [plan] A canvas camera fixture painted once can pass isolated capture checks while never providing continuing decoded video.
- [plan] Scroll drivers must remeasure after content reflow; an exact readiness wait cannot fix a stale target.
- [plan] A full-suite external-server guard must be audited against production subset probes and alternate local entrypoints.
- [plan] A successful feature-branch push does not satisfy this runner's main-ancestry delivery gate.
- [plan] Measure browser movement rate over the driven path, rather than requiring adjacent instrumented native-send timestamps to equal policy-clock boundaries.
- [plan] Publish app BUILD_ID after any verifier that rebuilds .next, and update isolated runner fixtures when adding transport ownership.
- [plan] Retain browser timeout evidence even when the isolated case and complete rerun pass
- [plan] Preserving another Pocket feature includes preserving its tested control adjacency.
- [plan] A red Vercel inspection can coexist with a successfully served renderer descendant
- [plan] A resumed SWE task can already contain its exact repair while the outstanding failure is an explicitly deferred operator chore.
- [plan] Use a dependency-appropriate readiness probe for a focused production harness.
- [plan] Inspect actual upstream paths after a rebase, even when the commit title names another feature.
- [plan] Read an empty fetch response body in the page itself when browser protocol body retrieval is unavailable.
- [plan] A browser can have zero pageerror events while an expected optional-endpoint 404 breaks a strict console-error gate.
- [plan] Membership updates can precede the scheduled canvas clear; independently wait for rendered state.
- [plan] A fixed canvas inside Home's animated page is not viewport-fixed; verify its browser geometry and portal it to the body.
- [plan] In an independent ws client, assert the received protocol close frame separately from TCP close completion and cross-socket event order.
